    /// Downloads this environment's transaction history as a CSV file.
    ///
    /// Scoped and filtered exactly as the JSON environment transaction listing
    /// is (`since`/`until`/`q`), but unpaginated and streamed: the whole
    /// filtered result set leaves in one response, one internal page at a
    /// time, rather than one caller-facing page of it. There is no upper
    /// bound on how large the file can be. Columns: `transactionId`,
    /// `chargePointId`, `evseId`, `connectorNumber`, `startedAt`,
    /// `endedAt`, `energyWh`, `idTokenLabel` — the same spellings the JSON
    /// transaction endpoints use for the same figures. Cost is deliberately not a
    /// column — it can legitimately be unavailable or "no tariff assigned"
    /// per transaction, which does not fit a column every row must answer the
    /// same way; fetch it per transaction from
    /// `GET /v1/transactions/{transactionId}/cost` instead. Any text cell
    /// that could be interpreted as a spreadsheet formula (a leading `=`,
