    /// Changes the tariff applied to a currently-running transaction.
    ///
    /// Distinct from [`assign_tariff`], which changes what future transactions
    /// pick up rather than this one. Only works while the transaction is still
    /// open — one that has already ended is refused with `404` rather than
    /// recomputed against the new tariff. The transaction need not already
    /// have a tariff assigned: this always sets `tariffId` as its current
    /// one, whether or not one was set before.
    ///
    /// The response does not itself compute a cost: `status` is the charging
    /// station's own answer to the change request, passed through verbatim,
    /// or `"unsupported: .."` / `"unreachable: .."` when the request never
    /// reached the station at all. Poll
